  "content_en": "Chapter One: First Married to the Prince's Mansion The three of them walked together playfully, and only restrained themselves a little in front of the princess's courtyard. Su Qi told Luo Xue that the princess’s yard was actually the prince’s yard. Luo Xue raised her head and observed carefully. The building with red walls and glazed roof tiles looks magnificent in the spring scenery. \"Are you all here?\" It was Fourth Lady Lianhua's voice. \"I didn't even say anything in the garden just now.\" \"Did Zhu Ling take out his anger on you again?\" Su Qi had pity in his eyes. Lian Hua shook his head and smiled, \"No, really not.\" \"She is used to bullying you! You just don't know how to resist! It's not her hometown anymore, this is our land!\" Su Qi was angry and hated Lian Hua's cowardice, but there was nothing he could do about it. \"Su Qi, I appreciate your kindness.\" Lian Hua turned his attention to Luo Xue. \"I heard that my sister met an assassin last time. I wonder if she was hurt?\" She returned the favor with a bright smile, \"Thank you for your concern, sister, and thank you to Xi Yi.\" As he said that, he turned to look at Xi Yi behind him, feeling a deep sense of gratitude in his heart. \"Madam, I told you that the assassin's left arm holding the sword was injured, which gave Xi Yi the chance.\" Xi Yi explained. A complex expression flashed across the face of the fourth lady Lian Hua, and she breathed a sigh of relief, \"No matter what, there is always a near miss.\" Yan Shu raised his slender hands, gently touched her temples, frowned slightly and said, \"Let's go in.\" Su Qi looked at Yan Shu and stretched out his hand to support her, \"I must have been standing for too long, and my body can't bear it.\" \"Yes, let's go in.\" Lian Hua echoed knowingly. We crossed the vermilion threshold and walked together to the front hall. A cup of tea exudes a faint fragrance on the Kang table with a bronze statue of rosewood. Princess Ting Ning was sitting on the edge of the Kang, and when she saw Luo Xue and others entering the room, she said with a smile in her eyes: \"The pieces of cloth for my sisters are on the table on the west side. Tell me which one you like, and I will go and discuss the new clothes.\" She glanced at the crowd without revealing any trace, and there was no trace of the second lady Zhu Ling. It would be better if this girl didn't cause trouble. Su Qi held the inkstone and Luo Xue followed Lian Hua and walked to the west side. Su Qi symbolically picked up two pieces of cloth and said, \"Sister, Yanshu and I have chosen these two pieces.\" Ting Ning still smiled, \"There are still many pieces of cloth, so there is no need to be formal. Luo Xue, follow me to the inner room and see if you like the fabric I selected for you.\" \"Okay.\" Luo Xue really couldn't guess about the princess. Most of the time, her behavior is elegant, her manners are dignified, and she is always warning the concubines of her determination to defend her status. He had clearly stated that he had no intention of peeping, so why would he still... I just hoped that he was overthinking it. Aren't there Xiao happy and Xi Yi behind him? \"Sisters, after you have finished selecting, please tell Dongyun and Lianhua, don't forget to bring back some pieces of fabric for Zhuling. Sister Luo Xue and I will excuse you for now.\" After saying that, he walked steadily towards the inner room. Luo Xue followed, and it was only a few steps away. Princess Ting Ning took Luo Xue's hand and walked to a mahogany round table. Xinshou picked up a piece of cloth and compared it with Luo Xue. \"The fabric really suits my sister.\" \"Thank you, sister.\" Luo Xue responded, but did not take the cloth. Seeing Luo Xue's embarrassment, Ting Ning smiled lightly and called to the maid behind Luo Xue: \"Xi Yi, Xiao Xi, help Luo Xue hold the cloth.\" \"Yes!\" Xiao Xi and Xi Yi walked to the table, picked up the cloth, and retreated behind Luo Xue. \"Sister, would you like to chat with me?\" As he said this, he looked at Xiao happy and Xi Yi and frowned slightly. Luo Xue understood that some words could not be heard by the servants. She was uneasy in her heart, but her face was calm. She turned her head and smiled, \"Take the cloth back. I will have a chat with my sister.\" After dismissing the maids around her, Luo Xue stood silently. The princess sighed softly, \"Let's go for a walk outside, it's a bit boring here.\" After walking out of the inner room, only the princess's maid Dongyun was left in the front hall to take care of things... The breeze was gentle, weeping willows and thin willows were leaning on the river bank, and clusters of red flowers were dotted on the clear blue sea. Along the way, no one disturbed the silence. \"Sister, don't blame Zhu Ling for being so arrogant.\" Princess Ting Ning said, she always likes to be the first to get the upper hand. \"Luo Xue understands.\" \"It's okay if my sister doesn't blame her. After all, she is like this because she loves her father too much.\" Ting Ning walked forward with small steps, \"Are you curious why I favor Zhu Ling?\" Seeing Luo Xue's silence, her face did not change at all, and continued: \"I think you must want to know about the third lady of the palace?\" Now that she had gotten straight to the point, Luo Xue could only nod in agreement. \"Actually, I often feel helpless.\"There was a hint of sadness on Princess Ting Ning's face. \"Five years ago, the barbarians in the southwest launched a war and captured Dali in an attempt to expand to the center. The imperial court was furious and mobilized 80,000 troops to suppress the arrogant barbarian forces and drive them back. Since then, the imperial court has repeatedly intervened and suppressed the barbarians. Forced by helplessness, the barbarian leader selected four women from the Central Plains to take the names of piano, chess, calligraphy and painting, and study with his beloved little daughter. \"The smart Luo Xue knew who the princess was talking about. \"A year ago, when the time of paying tribute was approaching, the barbarian leader came to the capital with his youngest daughter Yelu Zhuling and four maids in the name of choosing a husband. Everyone knew that this was a marriage proposal forced by the barbarians to beg for mercy, but no one pointed it out. Facing the barbarian men who were surrendering before him, the Holy Emperor accepted them with all his face, arranged them in the palace, and scheduled a marriage selection meeting in half a month. \"A marriage selection meeting?\" \"Ting Ning smiled, \"The barbarians have a custom that when their daughter is ready to marry, she will find a few women of similar age to hold a marriage selection meeting. At the meeting, the women, like the men, have to sit on horses and gallop on the sand. Marry whoever has the ability to force her to dismount. \"Luo Xue somewhat understood what Su Qiguo meant when he said that the inkstone fell off the horse. \"Living in the palace, it is inevitable to have contact with the royal children. I have always liked the piano, and when I learned that a woman with excellent piano skills had come to the palace, I did not hesitate to go to Zhu Ling's place to listen to the piano. Zhu Ling, who has just begun to fall in love, likes his father from the bottom of his heart, and is secretly planning the upcoming marriage selection meeting. But what Nai Ye fell in love with was Keqin, a girl who played the piano. \"Sister, Luo Xue doesn't understand why it's not Sister Zhuling who plays the piano?\" \"How can Zhu Ling, who has been spoiled since childhood, learn these things from us?\" The barbarian leader was afraid that Zhuling would make a fool of himself, so he brought four maids with him. \"There was a bamboo forest all around, and the bright sunlight was blocked by green bamboos. Luo Xue followed Ting Ning, for fear of getting lost. \"At the marriage selection meeting, Zhu Ling took four maids, each sitting on a horse, and the five of them galloped side by side on the palace racecourse. Behind him were the master and several young princes. In terms of riding skills, there was no distinction between men and women. Just like in a conference on the battlefield, where is the dignity and humbleness? \"At this point, Ting Ning unconsciously covered her mouth and smiled, \"At that time, Zhu Ling probably thought that I would chase him, so he secretly turned around. Sure enough, I had already thrown away the others, but he didn't expect that my horse was following closely behind Ke Qin on the outside. Seeing that he was about to catch up, he kicked the horse's belly angrily. The horse was frightened, causing the horses around him to become restless. Zhu Ling hurriedly grabbed the reins and exerted control, but was thrown off the horse. He covered his nose to drive away the dust, only to find that the four maids around him were also thrown off the horse in the shock. \"The five panicked horses were already out of control, right?\" The princess shook her head, \"Yes, how can you still listen to others?\" The five horses were frightened, lost their footing, and ran away. However, Yan Shu took pity on him and fell unconscious after falling off the horse. He was stepped on several times by the horse while he was in coma. \"Sister Yanshu is weak. Is this the root cause of her illness at that time?\" \"\"Um. I felt sorry for that girl, she didn't remember anything when she woke up. \"After making an unhesitating promise, Princess Ting Ning added: \"Since the five women have fallen off the horse, the marriage selection meeting has naturally ended. From the stand, it seems that it was the result of my one move. I had no choice but to marry these women, including Yan Shu, who was unconscious at the time. \"Is this how several sisters got married?\" \"Who would have thought that five of the current prince's concubines were married together? \"There is nothing I can do about this, but having Keqin, a confidante, by my side means I have no regrets. Ting Ning smoothed her hair and said, \"Sister Luo Xue, in the final analysis, Zhu Ling is a pitiful person after all. And who woman who falls in love with me is not pitiful?\" She just doesn't know how to hide her jealousy. \"Sister, actually Luo Xue really didn't blame Sister Zhu Ling.\" \"Is it important whether she is to blame or not? She is just the concubine of the Fifth Prince. \"Many times I wonder, is it lucky or unlucky for a woman to marry into a prince's palace and live a life of fine clothing and fine food? In the eyes of my daughter, the greatest happiness is to find a husband who is as she wishes, and the husband and wife respect each other and support each other throughout this life. But women in the palace are destined not to have such happiness, so what if they get the Lord's love? Just like Keqin who once won the favor of her master. \"I could tell that the princess was going to say something else, so Luo Xue didn't interrupt. \"You must really want to know what happened to Keqin, right? \"Ting Ning's eyes became wandering. \"Let's continue talking about the marriage selection meeting.. That day...\" Before Ting Ning finished speaking, she heard a rush of heavy footsteps not far behind her. The sound came first before anyone arrived. It was Dongyun, the princess's personal maid, \"Princess, it's not good, it's not good. \"What's causing such a panic?\" \"The second lady was drunk, causing a scene in the small village in the middle of the lake, and...\" Dongyun was panting and out of breath. Did Zhuling really get into trouble? \"What?\" What else? \"The expression on the princess's face changed from sunny to rainy. \"She also... also set fire to... the small building in the middle of the lake...\" \"Then how is the fire now? \"The person who spoke was Luo Xue. Thinking of Xiao Xi and Xi Yi, she couldn't help but worry. \"Fortunately, the fire stopped in time. The prince could not find the seventh lady. I heard that the seventh lady and the princess were together, but you were nowhere to be seen, so I sent me to find you. \"As soon as the voice stopped, a smile appeared on the princess's face again, \"Sister, I think we should go back first. I'm afraid this bamboo forest scenery is something we can't appreciate today. \"",
